<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mongol invasions of Georgia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1220">1220</a>–<a href="/years/1243">1243</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mongol invasions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> began with raids by the generals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebe">Jebe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a> in 1220–1222, which defeated the Georgian armies of King George IV. A full invasion in the 1230s overran the kingdom, and in 1243 Queen Rusudan accepted Mongol overlordship. Georgia remained a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-v">George V</a> restored its independence in the fourteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongol-invasions-of-georgia.jpg" alt="Mongol invasions of Georgia" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: gallica.bnf.fr · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HAYTON,_Fleur_des_histoires_de_la_terre_d%27Orient.(3).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
